  "timing_contract": [
    "All offsets are measured from one stage outer entry before Python loads and preflight.",
    "Admit no later than preflight_seconds; run for at most work_max_seconds and never beyond work_stop_absolute_offset_seconds.",
    "The absolute work-stop offsets are not latest-spawn offsets. There is no new full work allowance after those offsets.",
    "Retain the original bounded WNOWAIT leader anchor, owned group termination and reap, then group-absent verification; cleanup budget remains five seconds.",
    "compile retains 15 seconds after cleanup to write/validate evidence; others reserve five seconds.",
    "The outer wrapper must provide terminal exit and total wall receipts. A clean inner receipt without matching outer exit and elapsed bound is not acceptance."
  ],
  "resource_contract": [
    "One inherited CPU selected by the already-reviewed supervisor projection; make and Verilator jobs each fixed at one.",
    "AS, CPU and FSIZE are per process/file hard limits inherited through the owned process group, not aggregate subtree limits.",
    "Generation deliberately includes native make hier_verilation, sibling Perl wrapper and child Verilator processes in the same owned group; it must not invoke a C++ compiler.",
    "Aggregate output tree/log ceilings are postflight acceptance soft limits; no hard aggregate tree-space claim.",
    "Runtime has a 96MiB retained work-tree cap inherited from compile; its 1MiB new-output/log allowance is not a 1MiB cap on the compiled tree.",
    "Leader /proc samples identify one PID/starttime only; they do not measure child compilers' CPU/RSS.",
    "RUSAGE_CHILDREN is read after cleanup in a dedicated stage process; maxrss is cumulative peak, not a difference or a sampled subtree peak.",
    "Run tree inventory may retain pre-existing compile files up to32MiB; its inherited FSIZE4MiB hard limit still applies only to newly written files, and run must leave the prior work-tree inventory identical."
  ],
  "hierarchy_required_evidence": [
    "Exactly one specialized micro_leaf block in child __hierMkArgs.f: original name micro_leaf, --lib-create specialized_name, --hierarchical-child 1, and decoded -GSTEP=3. Record actual specialized name rather than assuming mangling.",
    "Vmicro_top_hier.mk exists with nonempty VM_HIER_LIBS naming a separately generated V<specialized_name>/lib<specialized_name>.a; top Vmicro_top.mk includes it.",
    "The top args file loads the generated leaf wrapper before the original tiny.sv and identifies the specialization via --hierarchical-block.",
    "Generated leaf .sv is a protected-library wrapper with chandle handle__V and actual create/combo_update/seq_update/final DPI calls; the top generated C++ invokes those wrapper imports.",
    "Independent leaf generated C++ contains the sequential state transition; the top generated C++ retains boundary calls, not an inlined substitute for the leaf body.",
    "After compile, the separate child archive exists with nonzero bytes and SHA-256. Actual log shows child compilation and top executable link. The fixed @-silent archive rule and VM_HIER_LIBS dependency explain its inclusion; absence of an echoed archiver command is not itself failure.",
    "Snapshot size/SHA/mode of every generated artifact, selected boundary text and exact build/link log. Merely passing --hierarchical or producing correct numbers is insufficient."
  ],
  "dpi_and_isolation_evidence": [
    "Explicit top-level SV exports hm_read_count, hm_read_delta, hm_set_delta have generated DPI declarations, C entrypoints, export registration and scope dispatch; record them separately from protectedlib boundary DPI.",
    "The two Vmicro_top objects use distinct VerilatedContext objects and identical model name dual; exact top scope dual.micro_top must exist in each context and resolve to distinct pointers.",
    "Every C++ call explicitly selects its context and DPI scope; writes alter only that top's delta, and reads agree with its public count and independent expected state.",
    "Interleaving: A delta5 ticks17 including unsigned wrap case; B delta11 ticks32. Required checkpoint counts A137/B455. Reset A alone to7 preserves B455; destroying A must leave B readable and able to tick to469.",
    "This tests TOP export routing plus actual leaf state reached through ordinary ports and protectedlib handles. It does not claim a direct exported function inside the leaf or arbitrary hierarchical memory DPI access."
  ],
  "expected_run_stdout": [
    "HOST93_MICRO_SCOPE_OK same_name=dual.micro_top distinct_context=1 distinct_model=1 distinct_scope=1",
